WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.980
Mt. Fuji on New Year's?

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.990
Or the horizon at sunset.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.480
That kind of beauty, you know?

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:13.910
And you're always alone at the 
store with this boss of yours?

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.250
When we don't have clients, yeah.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:22.370
This blond-haired, blue-eyed, multilingual, 
sweets-loving, incomparably beautiful boss?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.120
Well, yeah.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.220
Trade places with me!

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.310
Huh?

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.720
I'm so jealous of your job!

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.860
<i>Seigi-kun, do you know about the 
rocky outcrops on the Miura Peninsula?</i>

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.650
<i>If you're interested, why don't 
we go together sometime?</i>

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.620
What are you looking at?

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.970
When did you exchange 
numbers with Tanimoto-san?

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.560
<b>...go together...</b>

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.560
Why does all the good stuff 
keep happening to you?

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.350
You've already got Tanimoto-san.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.850
Let me have your boss!

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.320
Are you under the impression 
my boss is a woman, Shimomura?

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.180
Huh?

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.700
He's a man. His name is Richard.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.720
Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.790
Who asked for his full name?

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.730
Didn't I tell you my boss was a man?

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.750
No! And who wouldn't assume it's a woman 
when you said they like sweets?

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.310
Yeah, okay. Sorry.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.750
There must have been other 
comparisons you could've made.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.930
Like the Tokyo Tower as seen 
from the Yamanote Line.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.180
Well, I guess...

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.360
He's like a living jewel.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.950
<u>Episode 4</u>
<b>The Fighting Garnet</b>

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:16.670
Does that red bean jelly 
go with royal milk tea?

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.620
You underestimate royal milk tea.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.060
You're a royal milk tea fanatic...

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:32.170
Today's client, Yamamoto-sama, 
will be arriving soon.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.910
Please prepare for her arrival.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:36.900
Got it. She's coming to look 
at engagement rings, right?

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:40.610
Yes. She's requested a garnet.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.790
That's unusual.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.660
I thought engagements rings used diamonds.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.660
Why do you think that?

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.980
Why? Well, I've never really thought about it...

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.790
Why <i>do</i> engagement rings use diamonds?

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.260
Think about it.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.510
I'm Yamamoto. I called yesterday 
to make an appointment.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.390
We've been expecting you. Please come in.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.610
Make yourself comfortable.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.280
Thank you.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.120
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.120
I'm the owner, 
Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.670
I'm sorry for staring...

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:47.090
I've never seen someone with such 
a beautiful face. I was surprised.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.540
I was surprised when I first met him, too.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.610
Really?

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:56.190
They say you grow tired of a
pretty face after three days.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.230
But it's been two months 
since I started working here,

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.000
and I think he gets prettier every day.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.050
He still makes my heart flutter.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.630
Seigi, please fetch our guest some tea.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.450
Huh? Oh, certainly.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:11.980
I'll bring some right away.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.960
You said you were looking for 
a garnet for an engagement ring,

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.540
so I prepared several.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.050
Wow...

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:24.300
These are all garnets?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:28.970
"Garnet" is the generic term for a group 
of minerals with the same structure.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.120
Different compositions produce 
a variety of colors and luster,

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.980
and each has a different name.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.820
Because the most common red garnet

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.120
bears a resemblance to the fruit, in Japan...

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.820
They're called pomegranate gemstones.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.070
I did my homework.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.450
That's correct.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.700
There really are all kinds of colors.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.750
Is this one a tsavorite?

00:05:55.010 --> 00:06:00.080
No, this is a demantoid garnet.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.200
This is a tsavorite.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.300
I can't tell them apart at all...

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.760
My quick search online didn't get me very far.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.960
You're welcome to pick 
them up and look at them.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.390
May I?

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.950
But of course.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.130
In that case, I think I will.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:26.530
Even garnets are wonderful 
when you see them in person.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:28.970
"Even"?

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.700
This is delicious.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:37.160
This isn't store-bought, is it?

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.700
No. I make it in the kitchen here.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.520
My mother loves this stuff. 
She drinks it all the time.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.110
But I'm not sure hers is this good.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:50.220
We've also prepared some
 macarons to go with the tea.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.100
Please choose whichever ones you'd like.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.660
Then I'll take this one.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.020
Very well.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:02.980
I wish picking a stone for a ring
was as easy as picking a macaron...

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.760
Don't worry.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:09.740
If you'd like, I can find some to fit 
your budget for our next meeting.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:13.990
My budget? You're right...

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.370
I'll ask my boyfriend.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.690
Is your boyfriend a coworker of yours?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.590
It's amazing you both work 
for a foreign company.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.310
Are you fluent in English?

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.210
Seigi.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.920
No... I wouldn't say that.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.010
Speaking of, I'm surprised.

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.010
Your Japanese is great, Richard-san.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.320
Were you born and raised here?

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.090
In England, actually.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:45.060
Oh? Is de Vulpian an English name?

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.150
French. It's my mother's name.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.110
That's kind of cool.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.590
France and England...

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.990
So that's how this beauty was born.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:01.540
Don't you think he's pretty 
even when he's angry?

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.320
I've been wondering...

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.970
Have you ever been burned as 
a result of your careless speech?

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:19.960
Have I ever been burned
 by my careless speech?

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.100
No.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.480
Thank you.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.040
I believe I've gotten a good 
grasp on your outlook.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.500
Why is he mad?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.010
When you said outcrops, 
you meant geological formations?

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:49.830
Yeah. They look like shortcake, don't they?

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:50.630
Yeah.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.930
You can't get diamonds here.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:58.800
Natural diamonds have previously 
been discovered even here in Japan.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:08:59.610
What?

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.400
So you can get them in Japan?

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.640
Only tiny amounts, though.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.310
Anyway, what's this about diamonds?

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:11.630
Well, I've been thinking about why 
engagement rings are always diamonds.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:14.650
That's because of the power of marketing.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:15.760
Marketing?

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:16.570
Yeah.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.810
Unlike other gemstones, 
a single company has a monopoly

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:26.770
on their mining, distribution, 
processing, and sale.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:30.090
That company fabricated
 the value of diamonds.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.440
Fabricated their value?

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.250
Yup.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:38.020
"Only diamonds are suitable for important 
life events like celebrating a wedding."

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:43.390
"Diamonds are forever."

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.160
What? Really?

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:47.770
Richard?

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.880
Sorry. It's my boss.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:10:00.480
Richard

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:55.400
<i>Seigi, I'd like to take 
this opportunity to tell you</i>

00:09:55.400 --> 00:10:00.160
<i>everything I've thought about 
you since the day we met.</i>

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:04.110
<i>You are a ball of charm.</i>

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:10.840
<i>Every time I watch you work, 
my heart is filled with joy.</i>

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.260
What is this?

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.540
What's wrong, Seigi-kun?

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:17.130
O-Oh, nothing.

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:19.950
When should we go see the outcroppings?

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:22.580
Well, let me see...

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.910
I'm free most weekends.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:25.930
What about you?

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:37.530
Richard, do you have a minute?

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:39.280
What is it?

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.660
It's about the message 
you sent me the other day.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.200
What about it?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:48.620
It's, uh... nothing.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.910
I see.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.390
These are rhodolite garnets.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.970
I thought you might like them.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:08.270
I guess even garnets can 
be as beautiful as rubies!

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.020
<i>Even garnets are wonderful.</i>

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:14.480
Even garnets...?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.240
Garnets are said to be one of 
the world's oldest gemstones.

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:25.410
These stones formed in the earth 
over 100 million years ago.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.870
That long ago?

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:27.830
Yes.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.120
They're more affordable than rubies.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.750
I think a garnet is the perfect 
match for you, Yamamoto-sama.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:37.750
It's like the gemstone version of you.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.970
I know I'm not a ruby.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:48.600
Huh?

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:51.940
Listen... Can I ask you something?

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:54.150
Anything.

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:56.770
Have you ever benefited from your looks?

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.360
They say beautiful women 
have an advantage, right?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.750
So the same must be true 
for handsome men, right?

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:06.630
I'm flattered if you're 
complimenting my appearance,

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.950
but it's caused more harm than good.

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:17.420
As someone who isn't beautiful, I can 
definitely say pretty people are better off.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:21.560
Aren't gemstones of undesirable
 colors and shapes

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:25.430
used for industrial purposes 
or turned into paint?

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:30.310
People like me are no different
 from those stones.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.440
You're right.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:35.610
Gemstones are evaluated according 
to a number of criteria,

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:38.320
<b>Carats

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.320
judged, and assigned a price.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.580
But rather than being bound by 
inflexible criteria or preconceptions,

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:47.460
you seek a garnet for your engagement ring.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.950
I sense strong conviction in you.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:55.480
Therefore, I also believe that a garnet 
is the perfect gemstone for you.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:58.710
And what do you know about me?

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:01.690
What do I know about you, Yamamoto-sama?

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:02.570
Yes.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:06.050
If a garnet is so perfect for me,
then what kind of person am I?

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.300
But that's ridiculous...

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.620
You can stay out of this.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:13.020
Yamamoto-sama...

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.810
During the day, you work with flowers.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.290
You're good with your hands, 
and you enjoy handicrafts.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:19.680
You live with your parents.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.760
And recently, something happened 
that you haven't gotten over.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:26.050
How did I do?

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.030
How did you know?

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:34.700
I don't believe it...

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:45.550
My scent?

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.900
Yes.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:50.090
You always have the smell 
of fresh flowers about you,

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:53.350
unlike what you'd get with perfume.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:57.190
I mean no offense, but the second 
clue was the state of your hands.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:03.310
People who work with water get 
chapped hands this time of year.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:06.400
Like at a flower shop, for example.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:11.660
I reasoned that you must enjoy 
handicrafts based on your accessories.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.820
How did you know I live with my parents?

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:16.660
During our first meeting...

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.170
My mother loves this stuff. 
She drinks it all the time.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:22.580
Also, statistically speaking,

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:27.270
it's not unusual for a woman 
your age to live at home.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:33.510
Forgive me if any of that was presumptuous.

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.170
Amazing...

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:39.110
Um... Can I ask you something?

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:41.320
About why I lied?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.160
Yeah.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:45.280
Because I'm not beautiful.

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:46.860
Uh...

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:53.370
I was dumped by my boyfriend of seven years.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:56.350
He found a younger girlfriend.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:15:00.370
Of course he'd prefer a younger bride.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:04.170
So you wanted to buy a ring?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:10.820
I doubt anyone will give me a ring with 
a gemstone on it as long as I live,

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:12.550
so I thought I'd buy one for myself.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:16.510
I guess you could call it retail therapy.

00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:18.500
Why a garnet?

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:24.700
My birthday is in January. 
My birthstone is garnet.

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.400
Ah, so that's it.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:32.780
I first learned about my 
birthstone in middle school.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:35.210
I wasn't that happy about it.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.410
I wondered why it couldn't 
be a ruby or diamond.

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:45.440
My name is Mito, written with the 
characters for "beautiful person."

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.290
Huh?

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:49.230
It's like a punishment, isn't it?

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:52.920
I wish I could've actually 
been born beautiful instead.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:56.640
Hey, I'm sure you'll find a nice guy eventually.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:57.870
Seigi.

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:01.810
I know my commercial value.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.180
Your commercial value?

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:06.400
I'm not a diamond or a ruby.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:10.980
And garnets signify hard work
 and perseverance.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.490
That's perfect for me.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.270
Yamamoto-sama.

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:20.370
Gemstones stay with you longer than lovers.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:25.370
When you feel more strongly that you're 
purchasing rather than choosing one,

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.470
it may be a good idea to take your time.

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:32.470
I know what I'm doing is ridiculous.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.860
But I've made up my mind to buy one.

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:42.890
Why did you say that?

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:45.860
Yamamoto-san wanted to buy a ring.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.590
Gemstones don't always make people happy.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.780
But aren't gemstones mirrors 
that reflect their owners?

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:58.690
When someone is confused about 
what exactly it is that they want,

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:00.650
I don't recommend making a purchase.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:13.230
Richard...

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:15.630
Yamamoto-san?

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:18.350
I'm sorry. I know it's late.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.060
What's wrong?

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:24.310
I've decided not to buy a garnet after all.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:25.460
What?

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:27.690
I just can't...

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:36.440
I'd finished work and was on my way home...

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:45.820
when I saw my ex picking out an 
engagement ring with his new girlfriend.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:51.170
The moment I saw it, 
I wondered what I was doing.

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:55.880
Even if I buy a garnet,
 it'll only make me feel miserable.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:02.470
Are you familiar with the 
legends surrounding garnets,

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.660
apart from their meaning as gemstones?

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:06.430
No.

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:12.180
Garnets have been ripe with legend 
since the days of yore.

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:15.280
They appear in a number of stories.

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:21.110
In Ancient Rome, soldiers kept
 red garnets as talismans.

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:23.250
Like protective charms?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.160
Yes.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:28.320
People used them to pray for victory 
and a safe return home.

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:31.920
I believe the same is still true 
two thousand years later.

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.710
After all, life is a battle.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:35.800
A battle?

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:41.340
For example, when searching 
for a companion in life...

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:44.680
If an opponent appears, it means a fight.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:49.620
In such battles, I believe rather 
than youth or beauty,

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:53.900
hard work and perseverance 
are your best weapons.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:59.410
Of course, you're also free 
to choose not to fight.

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:05.850
But I see you as a warrior 
who stands her ground.

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:07.660
A w-warrior?

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:12.910
Yamamoto-sama, you wanted a garnet.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:16.400
Not any other gemstone, but your birthstone.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:20.930
You say you're not a diamond or a ruby,

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.750
but you don't shy away from that.

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:28.760
That proves you've given
great thought to who you are.

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:32.550
That you want to win, 
and that you want to survive.

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:34.890
That you have the will to fight.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.750
Thank you.

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.960
I'm sorry. That was embarrassing.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:03.930
Isn't it your choice whether 
to believe it was embarrassing

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.720
or to insist it was charming?

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:15.400
It's gotten quite late.
I'll treat you to dinner.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:16.770
Huh?

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:19.650
I'd also like to speak with you.

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.660
Okay...

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.850
Seigi, about the message I sent you...

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:39.920
Do you now understand the effect 
that careless words can have?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.170
Huh?

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:46.560
Words like "beautiful" and 
"pretty" are compliments,

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:48.550
but they're also used to judge.

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:51.910
Even the most innocent and beautiful words

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:55.180
can be interpreted quite differently
 than how you intended,

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.860
and your appraisal can hurt someone.

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:04.400
I upset her by talking about 
how pretty you are...

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.340
If you keep speaking 
and acting the way you do,

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:11.200
there will eventually be a hefty price to pay.

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:15.710
I'm really sorry.

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:19.030
I'm just glad you understand.

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.710
Thank you for waiting.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:25.720
Here's your strawberry parfait.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:29.020
Now, let us continue our meal.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.940
Meal?

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:45.190
Delivery!

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:48.950
A pomegranate tree, huh? 
Sounds just like Yamamoto-san.

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:51.740
So she's really not buying a stone after all?

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:52.410
No.

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:57.440
She's going to stay true to herself 
and try to become a fighter.
